Pending packaging follow-ups
============================

Repack for +dfsg (not urgent)
-----------------------------

Only real DFSG violations need removing; everything else (Windows-only C++
modules, PowerShell, .psd/.vsdx sources, templates, .NET helpers) is free and
unused by the agent-only build, so it can stay in the tarball.

Must remove (DFSG #2 - prebuilt binary, no source):
  installers/installer-NSCP/wixca.dll      PE32 DLL (WiX 2.0.5325.0, CPL-1.0)

The license itself is fine (confirmed by upstream); the violation is only the
missing source form in the tarball.

Review (borderline, not installed, safe to drop):
  docs/source/realtime-monitoring.vsdx     Visio file, never installed

Log to the journal instead of a file (evaluate)
-----------------------------------------------

The unit runs the agent with --log-backend threaded-file, so it writes
/var/log/nsclient/nsclient.log, rotated by debian/nsclient.logrotate. The
service also writes every line to stdout, so the journal already holds a
second copy of the whole log. Logging to the journal alone, with --log-backend
console (a service with no flag picks threaded-file itself), would drop that
duplicate, the rotation snippet and the log directory in nsclient.tmpfiles,
and would give the usual journalctl -u filtering and retention.

What is missing before switching: nscp tags no priority. Every line goes to
stdout, errors included, so the journal files them all as "info" and
journalctl -p cannot filter by level until upstream emits the sd-daemon(3)
level prefix.

check_nscp is unaffected either way: its error count is kept in memory, it does
not read the log file.
